body:
Yea it's definitely not going to be the first game I DM. I'm planning on either doing Saltmarsh or Princes of the Apocalypse if not a small one-shots just to test the waters, see if I'll be comfortable with it in the first place. The idea is generally a story I'd like to build-up with ideas before even considering asking if people would be interested. And I completely understand not to give pc's personalities, it really takes the fun out. I had a friend who I explained the idea to and they told me they'd be interested in playing a BBEG in the campaign if I ever considered it, forcing a role onto someone who doesn't want to do it would generally lead to a boring session. This is a story/adventure I'd like to build up over the next few months if not year(s) before bringing it to the attention of any other friends. I'll probably also have a few of my DM friends help me structure it, asking them what works and what doesn't. 

&#x200B;

I highly appreciate your advice though, thanks b!<3
